# BLOOM, black key 7: pressed, it swells in; held, the knobs shape it (LEVEL, LENGTH, HEIGHT: the root, an
# octave over, two; FIFTH) and it stays so; PULSE's page reset (SEL twice) puts it back as made. A 0.16 or
# 0.17 journey (no BLOOM) comes with it as made. No clicks, no clips. Audio in bloom.wav.
autoplay 0
wait 300
wav bloom.wav
expect bloom0 90
expect bloom2 1
key b6 down
wait 100
turn K1 -10
turn K2 10
turn K3 -1
turn K4 20
wait 100
shot bloom_hold.png
key b6 up
expect bloom0 70
expect bloom1 84
expect bloom2 0
expect bloom3 104
wait 6000
tapkey b6
wait 3000
key b6 down
turn K3 3
key b6 up
expect bloom2 2
tapkey b6
wait 12000
tap ENV
turn SELECT 4
tap SEL
tap SEL
wait 100
expect bloom0 90
expect bloom1 64
expect bloom2 1
expect bloom3 64
wavstop
expect clips 0
legacy017
wait 500
expect journey 4
expect vcur 3
expect bloom0 90
expect bloom1 64
expect bloom2 1
expect slot1 1
expect jr_playing 0
